       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe maximum.\n\nAcetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6 g per day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g per day, and many institutions cap it at 3 g. A single 2000 mg dose is also higher than the standard 500\u20131000 mg. At 6 g per day there is a real risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily**, for 3 g per day. This is a common regimen.\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily**, for 4 g per day. This is the standard maximum.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, for 2.6 g per day.\n- **2000 mg per day or some other total**, if that was what you meant.\n\nIf you really do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
