       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 6 g per day is 50% above the 4 g maximum, and I can't think of a clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. It could cause serious liver injury, and the patient is the one who would bear that harm. I'd rather not put it into the system, where it could be given before anyone catches it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g per day)\n- 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g per day)\n- 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2.6 g per day)\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the standard maximum, please talk to the pharmacist or your attending first. Any order above the maximum should go through their review. If they approve a specific regimen, I can enter it with a note recording who approved it.\n\nIf the pain isn't controlled at the standard maximum, I can help you add another drug or a multimodal option."
